    "prose": "Rain beat harder beyond the gallery entry, and wind drove spray against the open doorway. Aya and Mert held the same restored mosaic between them, still level and intact.\n\nThe fixed display mount waited in the alcove. Aya studied the remaining distance. Her arms ached with the temptation to finish quickly, but she remembered the tiny shift on the ramp.\n\n“Mert, help me keep it level all the way to the mount,” she said. “Same slow pace?”\n\nHe met her eyes and nodded. “Same pace.”\n\nAya stepped through the wide open gallery door into the display alcove, keeping both hands steady on her side.\n\nMert stepped through the wide open gallery door into the display alcove, matching her careful movement.\n\nThe mosaic panel passed through the wide open gallery door into the display alcove, supported between them in their two-person hold.\n\nThey stopped before the mount. Neither tried to take control.\n\n“Down together,” Aya said.\n\n“Together,” Mert answered.\n\nAya and Mert lowered the mosaic panel onto the fixed display mount at the same careful speed. They eased their hands away only after it rested securely. The restored panel remained intact, now displayed where it belonged.\n\nFor a moment, Aya listened to the rain hammering outside. Then she turned to Mert.\n\n“I wanted to carry it alone at first,” she said. “That would have been a mistake. Your help—and both of us being careful—got it here safely.”\n\nMert watched her as she spoke. His shoulders loosened, though he only gave a small nod.\n\n“We did all right,” he said.\n\nAya looked back at the intact mosaic. “We did.”",
